---
title: Greek Salad
course: Side
servings: 4
locale: en
difficulty: easy
cuisine: Greek
---

Slice the @red onion{0.5} as thinly as possible. Whisk the @red wine vinegar{2%tbsp} with half the @olive oil{6%tbsp} and stir into the onion. Leave to soak for at least ~{20%minutes}.

Cut the @sweet tomatoes{10%small} into generously bite-sized chunks, sprinkle with @salt{pinch}, and leave for ~{10%minutes}.

When ready to serve, roughly chop the @cucumber{1} into chunks and arrange on a platter. Add the tomatoes, onions (reserving any soaking liquid), @kalamata olives{25} and @capers{1%tbsp}(drained, or rinsed if packed in salt). Whisk the rest of the oil into any liquid remaining in the onion bowl, then use this to dress the salad, along with most of the @fresh oregano{3%sprigs}(or generous pinch dried oregano).

Crumble the @feta{150%g} on top, and sprinkle with the remaining oregano to serve.